BarData: property borderSkipped
Borders left undrawn

A boolean scalar or a character vector. This setting is used to avoid
drawing any given border of each bar. As a boolean value, false
does not skip any borders and true skips drawing all borders. As
a character vector, it can take any of the following values:
'start', 'end', 'middle', 'bottom',
'left', 'top', and 'right'. 'middle' is
only valid on stacked bars, in which case the borders between stacked
bars are skipped.


