ScatterChart: obj = ScatterChart (X, Y)
ScatterChart: obj = ScatterChart (..., Name, Value)
Create a ScatterChart object.

obj = ScatterChart (X, Y) returns a
ScatterChart object, in which X and Y define the
coordinates along the x-axis and y-axis, respectively.

X must be a nonempty NxP numeric matrix, where each column
corresponds to a separate dataset and each row corresponds to an element
of the bubble chart defining its position along the x-axis.

Y must be a nonempty NxP numeric matrix, where each column
corresponds to a separate dataset and each row corresponds to an element
of the bubble chart defining its position along the y-axis.

obj = ScatterChart (..., Name, Value)
returns a ScatterChart object with the properties of each dataset
specified by one or more Name, Value pair arguments.
Name can be any property name of a ScatterData object and
Value must correspond to the data type(s) and values accepted by
that property. Type help ScatterData for more details on the
available properties.

Specifically for the properties that accept a Color object as
their input value, besides the Color object you may also parse to
the ScatterChart constructor the same values accepted by the
constructor of the Color object. However, if you choose to
manually modify the ScatterChart's properties using the dot
notation syntax, then you must assign a Color object to the
chosen property. Type help Color for more details on the
available syntax.

For properties that accept scalar values, you can pass a vector of the
same type with each element corresponding to a different dataset. For
properties that accept vectors, you can pass a matrix of the same type
with each row corresponding to a different dataset. Otherwise, the same
property value will be assigned to all datasets available in data.
For properties accepting a character vector, you need to pass a
cellstring array for multiple datasets, whereas for properties that can
take mixed types of scalar values (i.e. either boolean and character
vectors), you need to pass a cell array with each element corresponding
to a different dataset.


